  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure over the East Coast will continue to dominate the\nregion and allow for dry, seasonable weather. This system will\nmove southwest through the central Appalachians and into the\nTennessee Valley on Monday. This will allow for a weak cold\nfront to enter the area before quickly washing out overhead. A\nnew high pressure system will enter from the north on Tuesday\nand settle over the New England states through at least\nThursday. Overall, the dry pattern is expected to continue for\nthe bulk of the week. The only main weather impacts may end up \nbeing this morning with some fog in Northwest Ohio and some\nfrost in extreme Northeast Ohio and Northwest Pennsylvania. The\nfog appears too limited for a headline. The frost is in zones\nthat have ended their growing seasons.",
